.Dd November 15, 2026
.Dt DTRACE_READ 2
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtrace_read
.Nd drain per-CPU DTrace rings
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Fn dtrace_read out max
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm copies up to
.Fa max
records from the per-CPU rings to
.Fa out
in round-robin CPU order and returns the number copied.
One call accepts at most 1024 records.
A record is 64 bytes: a 64-bit sequence number, a 64-bit monotonic timestamp,
four 64-bit probe arguments, a 32-bit syscall number, a 32-bit thread
identifier, a 16-bit CPU index and a 16-bit probe identifier.
.Pp
Rings are drop-on-full: a producer never overwrites a record the consumer has
not seen.
The drop count is reported by
.Xr dtrace_stats 2 .
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Er EINVAL
.Fa max
exceeds 1024 or the byte count overflows.
.It Er EFAULT
.Fa out
is not writable user memory.
.El
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
